                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" vertex="1" value="&lt;b&gt;Legend&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;solid line, open arrow: association (stored field), with role name and multiplicity&lt;br&gt;filled diamond: composition (the owner creates the part)&lt;br&gt;hollow diamond: aggregation (the part already exists)&lt;br&gt;dashed line, open arrow: dependency (parameter, return or local use)&lt;br&gt;solid line, hollow triangle: inheritance&lt;br&gt;dashed line, hollow triangle: realisation (implements)&lt;br&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt;boundary&amp;gt;&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;&amp;lt;control&amp;gt;&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;&amp;lt;entity&amp;gt;&amp;gt; as in the BCE slides. italics: abstract. {leaf}: final. underlined: static" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;dashed=1;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;">
                    <mxGeometry x="40" y="2194" width="600" height="170" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="n1" parent="1" vertex="1" value="&lt;b&gt;Encapsulation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fields are private and have no setters. A Customer or an Order changes state only through event methods that check the current state first (requireState / requireStatus)." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;dashed=1;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;">
                    <mxGeometry x="670" y="2194" width="560" height="100" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="n2" parent="1" vertex="1" value="&lt;b&gt;Dependency inversion&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;GameController depends on the GameView interface (not ConsoleUI) and only on the abstract Customer: the arrival list decides the types, so no customer class is named in the controller." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;dashed=1;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;">
                    <mxGeometry x="1260" y="2194" width="560" height="100" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="n3" parent="1" vertex="1" value="&lt;b&gt;Composition&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;GameController creates and owns its staff, statistics, tables and waiting queue (filled diamond). Menu creates its MenuItems (filled diamond)." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;dashed=1;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;">
                    <mxGeometry x="1850" y="2194" width="560" height="100" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="n5" parent="1" vertex="1" value="&lt;b&gt;Polymorphism, template method, Liskov&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The customer types only override the hooks satisfactionLossPerTurn(), getDiscountPercent() and pickDish(). The event methods are final {leaf}, so every type follows the same visit (checked by CustomerSubstitutionTest). The Critic always orders the most expensive dish." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;dashed=1;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;">
                    <mxGeometry x="2440" y="2194" width="560" height="130" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="n4" parent="1" vertex="1" value="&lt;b&gt;Not drawn&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The records TurnSnapshot, GameResult and ActionResult, private helper methods, and the dependencies that only pass a value (for example Waiter and Host on Table and WaitingQueue, Order and HappyHour on Money, GameController and ConsoleUI on GameConfig). GameController also keeps the Menu (attribute menu in the code) and ArrivalSchedule keeps its Customers." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;dashed=1;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;">
                    <mxGeometry x="40" y="2394" width="560" height="120" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>